WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.963
What to carry into the next two lessons.

2
00:00:02.243 --> 00:00:04.973
You now have a vocabulary and a decision rule.

3
00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:10.053
A workflow is code choosing the path with models doing bounded work at each step.

4
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:14.472
An agent is the model choosing the path inside a loop your code bounds.

5
00:00:14.752 --> 00:00:19.403
Autonomy is a dial, and the right setting is usually lower than the hype suggests.

6
00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:22.136
The four questions tell you when to turn it up.

7
00:00:22.416 --> 00:00:31.739
Lesson 2 makes the workflow side concrete: five patterns from the Anthropic post, each in a few lines of code, and how to verify each one’s output.

8
00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:43.645
Lesson 3 does the math on the agent side: why per-step reliability compounds, what a loop really costs, and what published measurements say about how long a task current agents can handle.
